>> Is that possible?  Is it possible for a boulder to be created over a
>> pit?  Or did I (probably) misremember, the course of events?
>> 
> 
> I know that mimics in Sokoban that are pretending to be boulders atop
> pits will not fall in and fill up the pits. Never seen anything where
> a boulder was created atop a pit.
> 
Interestingly a wizard mode check shows that breaking a WoDig won't create 
holes/pits under any boulders but neither does it remove the boulders. I'm 
not sure whether that's a bug or a deliberate limitation: zapping digging 
downwards while in the same place as a boulder gives "KADOOM! The boulder 
falls in!" so you again don't get a hole/pit but it does remove the 
boulder.

One way you can fall into a pit directly after pushing a boulder would be 
if the boulder was on top of a landmine. I guess maybe if you killed a 
giant who had escaped the landmine you could get that situation.


